# AI-NIDS-Project

An enterprise-ready AI-powered Network Intrusion Detection System (NIDS) prototype built with:
- Go for high-performance packet capture and flow analysis
- Python for ML feature engineering and anomaly scoring
- Prometheus + Grafana for real-time monitoring and dashboarding
- REST API and web dashboard for alert visualization
- Docker Compose for local deployment

The project demonstrates an end-to-end architecture for passive network traffic inspection using SPAN/mirror traffic, flow telemetry, AI-assisted anomaly scoring, and dashboard-based SOC monitoring.

## Architecture overview

```text
Production traffic
       │
       ▼
[Core switch / SPAN port]
       │
       ▼
[Go capture agent]
       │  packet + flow metrics
       ▼
[ML scoring service]
       │  anomaly score + alert decisions
       ▼
[REST API]
       │
       ├── Grafana dashboard
       ├── Web dashboard
       └── SIEM / alert log integration
```

## Features
- Passive packet capture from a mirrored interface
- Flow-level telemetry aggregation
- Protocol and payload feature extraction
- AI anomaly scoring with ML service
- REST API for alert and summary retrieval
- Web dashboard for SOC-style monitoring
- Prometheus + Grafana telemetry export
- Dockerized deployment

## Project structure
- `cmd/nids` — capture service entrypoint
- `cmd/api` — lightweight alert/summary API service
- `internal/api` — REST API logic and alert store
- `python` — ML training and attack simulation utilities
- `dashboard` — Prometheus, Grafana, and web dashboard files
- `docker-compose.yml` — local stack bootstrapping

## Quick start

### 1. Start the full stack

```bash
docker compose up --build
```

### 2. Access the dashboards
- Grafana: http://localhost:3000
- Web UI: http://localhost:8081
- Prometheus: http://localhost:9090
- API: http://localhost:8080/health

### 3. Train the model

```bash
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r python/requirements.txt
python python/train_model.py
```

### 4. Run the packet capture service directly

```bash
go run ./cmd/nids --iface eth0
```

### 5. Run the API service directly

```bash
go run ./cmd/api
```

